<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikh conquest of Kashmir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghan-sikh-wars">Afghan–Sikh Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> took place in 1819, when the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> took the valley from its Afghan rulers. Kashmir became a valuable province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, famed for its shawl industry. It was later lost after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> and transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikh-conquest-of-kashmir.jpg" alt="Sikh conquest of Kashmir" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See description · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Sikh-ruled_Kashmir,_given_by_General_Claude-Auguste_Court_to_Victor_Jacquemont,_1831.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
